WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.960
Hi everyone and welcome back to another video.&nbsp;
Today I thought I'd make something that I haven't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.640
done for a while on the channel and that is&nbsp;
a more of a personal video that's unscripted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.560
and sharing a bit more of my thoughts.&nbsp;
So I'm going to do a bit of a Q&amp;A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.880
answering some of the common questions&nbsp;
that I've seen popping up in the comments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.880
but I also asked my Patreon&nbsp;
supporters for some questions.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.960
I've written a few of those down in my&nbsp;
notebook here so I'll work through those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.120
as well as generally sharing what I've been&nbsp;
up to. I'm going to start with the question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.560
that I've used for the title of this video and it&nbsp;
was a comment that I received that asked me if I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.120
had ever failed a test. I've looked through&nbsp;
plenty of tests now on the channel so it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.480
only a natural kind of question and apart from&nbsp;
maybe my real analysis midterm, I do have one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.720
interesting story about failing tests but it's not&nbsp;
probably the kind of test that you would expect.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:59.440
So one test that made me cry as a teenager&nbsp;
was the New Zealand Full License Driving test.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:05.360
I took this when I was 16 and a half&nbsp;
and as the title says I failed it twice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.120
On my third try though I did pass so I have&nbsp;
my full license now but it wasn't without at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.920
least a little bit of misery along the way. In New&nbsp;
Zealand you have three tests before you get your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:22.000
driver's license. One is a theory exam that I got&nbsp;
a hundred percent on, the second one is a one hour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.600
driving test where you do all sorts of things&nbsp;
like three-point turns and various maneuvers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:34.320
that I also aced I got 100, but the third&nbsp;
test is the full license test where it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:40.640
only a 20-minute drive and you go through a bunch&nbsp;
of hazard detection things and general assessment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.680
of your driving. The first time taking the&nbsp;
test I did really well for the whole time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:51.520
hadn't done anything wrong, and we were driving&nbsp;
back to the testing facility to go over everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.440
and just on the last little corner&nbsp;
before getting to the destination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:02.400
I got done for going over the speed limit. I was&nbsp;
going probably between 55 and 60 when the speed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.080
limit was 50 there and I just can't even explain&nbsp;
that it was so out of character for me because I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.520
actually a really slow driver and anyone that&nbsp;
knows me would complain that I drive too slow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:19.600
so to have failed for going too fast is yeah kind&nbsp;
of ironic but um I think that nervous energy of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.800
being in a testing situation just bubbled over&nbsp;
right towards the end there and I wasn't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.120
thinking straight. You think I might have learned&nbsp;
my lesson though but the second time I took the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.000
test I did it in a different city, I did it in&nbsp;
Christchurch, whereas the first time I took it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.960
a pretty small town that didn't even have traffic&nbsp;
lights or multiple lanes or anything so it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.160
a very different style of driving to taking it&nbsp;
in a city but the second time I took the test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:50.240
again did really well for most of the time didn't&nbsp;
do anything wrong until the last intersection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.800
just pulling into the car park there was a stop&nbsp;
sign and I didn't stop properly at the stop sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.360
something that of course you have to do. Again&nbsp;
I think I just didn't deal well with the stress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.320
of being tested and watched while I'm driving&nbsp;
so that was that, got to be like Spongebob at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.320
boating school for a while but eventually got it&nbsp;
on my third try. A little taste of failure for me.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.360
This next question I must have had over&nbsp;
a hundred times now I get it all the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.640
someone asking me, 'where do you get all those&nbsp;
exam papers from?', 'How did you get special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:28.480
access?' and sometimes people even shout at me in&nbsp;
all caps with these really abusive comments saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.760
'why aren't you using gloves to handle these&nbsp;
precious documents?'. Something along those lines.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.320
So I just wanted to quickly say in the&nbsp;
descriptions of all those videos where I use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:44.240
original documents, exams, things like that, I do&nbsp;
always link to the sites where I get them from and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:50.560
I don't have any special access. I don't have the&nbsp;
original copy of Einstein's grades, rather I did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:56.480
enough research to find them on the ETH library&nbsp;
website, that's the university that Einstein had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:02.000
gone to. Doing research to find all those original&nbsp;
documents is probably the most time consuming part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:07.200
of some of my videos, there are documents that I&nbsp;
would love to cover but they just aren't available&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.480
online and not being able to travel to the&nbsp;
libraries in Europe and look through the archives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.640
I've never been able to cover those things so I&nbsp;
do really appreciate when the universities put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:24.480
them on digitized versions of the archives and&nbsp;
everything that I cover whether it's the exams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.840
the grades, or anything else, they're always&nbsp;
publicly available when I access them. I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.400
print them out the best I can on my little home&nbsp;
printer and then show them under the camera.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:39.680
One question I should address is the common one&nbsp;
asking if I have an Instagram account, the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.880
is no. I disabled my account quite a while ago&nbsp;
now and haven't really been on Instagram since.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:51.760
For me instagram didn't feel like a positive&nbsp;
place or a way to spend my time, I would get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:56.720
caught mindlessly scrolling through things and&nbsp;
I would often wish that I had enough willpower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:02.080
to get off and go read a book or do something&nbsp;
else. It's a platform that kind of made me feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:08.960
bad about myself so it felt hypocritical for&nbsp;
me to be posting photos and trying to grab your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:14.960
attention and try to make you stay on the app when&nbsp;
