00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:45.280
Pretty much everything that you'll see in the&nbsp;
film is handmade from felt so here's what some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:51.200
that looks like. There are little houses that our&nbsp;
characters live in including our main character X&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.920
who lives in this house here. X themself&nbsp;
came from this bit of felt here which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:01.840
I've painted with watercolors to give it that&nbsp;
coloring. Our other characters include numbers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:10.160
symbols and roman numerals, all complete with&nbsp;
their own unique accessories, hats, glasses, hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.840
pieces. A small piece like the scarf might only&nbsp;
get seen for a split second in the final video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:22.000
but it still took a lot of work to make. This&nbsp;
here is a little chalkboard that I made for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.080
fairground scene and these two windows are some&nbsp;
of my favorite assets, I modeled them off the four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:34.000
color theorem especially the example given on the&nbsp;
wikipedia page. The four color theorem states that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.400
you'll never need any more than four colors&nbsp;
to color in the regions of any map like this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:46.080
such that no two adjacent regions have the same&nbsp;
color. So I had to make sure when I was cutting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.360
out all of these pieces that no two regions of&nbsp;
the same color were touching and it was a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:57.280
tricky but I think I managed to do it right in the&nbsp;
end. So whenever I had any spare time I would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:02.960
sitting on the floor cutting things out, gluing&nbsp;
them together. The felt was then photographed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:09.840
some scenes have elements of real stop-motion but&nbsp;
for everything else the images got sent off to Ben&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.440
who brought them to life on the computer. I've&nbsp;
