00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:20.080
The next question I wanted to answer is one that&nbsp;
asked me to share a bit about my creative process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:25.600
making videos and I think this makes sense to talk&nbsp;
about after having shared the progress of Finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.920
X with you because I have a lot of thoughts about&nbsp;
maybe my philosophy when it comes to content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:38.000
creation and you know even a bit of confusion&nbsp;
there on what really is the best approach.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:44.400
Always a motto that I really liked is one that my&nbsp;
mum says which is 'minimum effort, maximum gain'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:51.200
and it kind of sounds a little bit rude almost but&nbsp;
I think it's kind of true especially with Youtube,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.800
social media and growth on these sorts of&nbsp;
platforms. It seems more important to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:03.040
putting out a lot of content that isn't quite&nbsp;
perfect rather than taking ages to upload real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:09.360
masterpieces and this is what you see with&nbsp;
my regular content. With my normal videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:15.440
they're far from perfect, they're often just made&nbsp;
entirely by myself and there are so many aspects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.560
that in hindsight could be a little better&nbsp;
but really if I think about it, what would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:27.120
the payoff be in terms of getting any extra&nbsp;
views if I spent you know many extra hours on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:33.440
transitions or fancy sound and things like that.&nbsp;
I kind of for the most part think nah don't go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:38.880
too fancy just put it up and people are there&nbsp;
for the core message anyway and me investing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:44.320
all that extra time probably won't result in&nbsp;
many more views or or that much more enjoyment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:51.040
So then why have I spent a year and a half&nbsp;
painstakingly slaving over this Finding X project?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:57.520
It is perfectionism to the level that every single&nbsp;
thing that you see in it has been through multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:02.720
sets of edits, has passed through multiple eyes&nbsp;
and had multiple opinions on if it's the very best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:09.440
thing for that particular spot and I really lived&nbsp;
and breathed every aspect of this project for so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:14.880
long now. Given that there are multiple people&nbsp;
involved in it as well I feel like I can't release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:20.240
any version of it that is less than perfect it's&nbsp;
been a lot of stress to do and i'm not convinced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:26.000
that after all of that that it would perform any&nbsp;
better than any other regular video on my channel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:31.440
For most videos on Youtube I don't believe&nbsp;
that there is any correlation between effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:37.520
and success as measured in views. I know that my&nbsp;
most viewed video is definitely the one that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:43.840
the least effort put into it and even some of my&nbsp;
ones in the top 10 most viewed you know they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:49.760
kind of ones that I didn't expect to do well, they&nbsp;
just took off maybe thanks to the statistics of;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:55.040
if you put out a lot of stuff at least maybe&nbsp;
something is bound to be good. I won't be upset&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:02.400
if Finding X gets less views than say this Q &amp; A,&nbsp;
it's possible, but that's not really what Finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:08.400
X is about. It's not a project that I undertook&nbsp;
to get max views, I think there are many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:13.360
roads I could have taken if that was the goal.&nbsp;
I think Finding X is something that I'm always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:18.640
going to be proud of. I think it looks really&nbsp;
beautiful, I think it's an approach to sharing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:24.800
math to people in a way that I haven't really seen&nbsp;
before and I really hope that you enjoy it too.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:30.960
In terms of my creative process for the rest of my&nbsp;
videos it starts off with quite a time-consuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:36.640
phase of research where I really like to&nbsp;
live in the topic for at least a few days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:41.280
I read everything about it that I can, maybe go&nbsp;
off on a tangent watching documentaries about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:46.640
the topic on Youtube, really soak up all the&nbsp;
knowledge about whether it's a certain country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:53.680
their exams or a certain character from history.&nbsp;
And then I try to condense that into a script,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:59.520
I only ever really script the face cam sections&nbsp;
of those videos. Usually that's the intro.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:04.800
For anything that's overhead I feel like I can&nbsp;
breathe a sigh of relief and just talk off the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:10.080
of my head in those sections because I know don't&nbsp;
have to worry about looking at the camera, looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:16.320
good or saying sentences without too many cuts&nbsp;
and things like that. I can really just drop all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:21.440
of the knowledge I know and it doesn't matter if&nbsp;
it comes out in a scrambled way. I can deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:28.160
editing it together to be a succinct story later.&nbsp;
To do that editing probably takes me about a day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:33.120
to a day and a half depending on how intensely&nbsp;
I'm working on it. I do the editing myself on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:40.160
my laptop using final cut pro and I still use&nbsp;
my canon g7x as my main camera. It's probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:45.360
one of the least professional cameras to use for&nbsp;
something like this especially as my channel grows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:50.560
but sometimes I joke that I don't want people&nbsp;
to see me in 4k especially if I have you know a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:55.280
pimple or a bad hair day or something I don't want&nbsp;
people to be able to zoom too close into that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.280 --> 00:14:00.800
I'm still trying to keep to that motto of keeping&nbsp;
things as simple as possible and my fairly minimal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:06.640
setup for these videos seem to have worked alright&nbsp;
so far with only a few complaints here or there.

